<div class="columnArticleClass two-layout-bg-white" id="oneColumnArticleTheme"><div id="sectionHeadingForOneColumnArticle"><div class="section-heading mb-4 container text-start" data-ste-element="Sites: Section Heading"><div><div class="row text-start"><div class="col col-md-8"><h2 class="header-focus"><span>Why SICAM P855?</span></h2></div></div></div></div></div><div class="text-start container multitextblock "><div class="row justify-content-left"><div class="col col-md-8"><p>The SICAM P855 is a power quality (PQ) recorder for comprehensive electrical parameter monitoring and reporting. It collects, displays and transmits key electrical variables such as AC current, AC voltage, power types and harmonics across diverse power systems.</p><p>Poor power supply quality not only negatively impacts operations and safety but also increases costs. The SICAM P855 addresses this by comprehensively acquiring and documenting supply quality parameters. Identify weak points and initiate measures to ensure stable, reliable power.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div id='1Ml7SoZ7ta8NW7zMncMymL' class='sitesThreeColTiles themed-component-wrapper' data-ste-section='three-col-tiles_2' data-ste-section-id='1Ml7SoZ7ta8NW7zMncMymL'>
